WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.310
- But I heard one time
that you were on like

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.870
I guess theater, you were doing theater,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.311
and you fell asleep on stage.

00:00:06.311 --> 00:00:08.190
(Jon laughs) Like your character
is supposed to be asleep,

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.810
but you actually fell asleep.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.510
- Yes, I fancy myself a
very professional actor.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.951
- Do you? (laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:00:13.951 --> 00:00:15.690
- But apparently that's not true.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.610
No, I was, one of my very first jobs

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.130
was in a Broadway show called
"Brighton Beach Memoirs."

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.540
It's a wonderful Neil Simon play.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.430
- Yeah, yep.
(audience applauds)

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.233
- An amazing, amazing writer.

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:31.950
And my character had to
fall asleep at one point.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.040
He had to go upstairs and
go to sleep in his room.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.790
But you have not experienced
terror until you realize

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.970
that you fell asleep
during the Broadway show

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:45.030
you're starring in. (chuckles) Um.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.640
Oh my goodness, 'cause I remember

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.490
there was an actor named Joe
Breen who, wonderful actor,

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.707
who was in, he was in "Galaxy Quest."

00:00:55.336 --> 00:00:57.510
And I remember just laying
there and he was sleeping,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.220
he was sleeping across from me,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.696
but he is a better actor
who fakes it, apparently.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.370
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.660
And I remember him,

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.279
and I remember just the
look on his face going,

00:01:09.279 --> 00:01:11.730
"Jon, Jon, Jon."

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.070
And his eyes got all huge.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.960
And then I was like,
"Huh, I wonder what's,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.106
I wonder what Joe's, what his problem is."

00:01:18.106 --> 00:01:18.939
- What's your problem? (laughs)

00:01:18.939 --> 00:01:23.040
- Exactly. And then, the
adrenaline shot of all time

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.040
went through my body
because I realized I was,

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.380
I had fallen asleep during the
play that I was supposed to.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.107
But thankfully, if you rehearse
enough, it's muscle memory.

00:01:32.107 --> 00:01:36.630
So, I leapt in, and the
monologue that I had to say,

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.380
thankfully, leapt into
my mouth, but that--

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.570
- Well, you had a nap.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:40.560
You should have felt fresh. (laughs)

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.073
- You're right. (laughing)
- Should have felt real fresh.

00:01:43.073 --> 00:01:43.906
- Yes, you're right, you're right.

00:01:43.906 --> 00:01:44.739
- There's nothing more terrifying

00:01:44.739 --> 00:01:46.530
'cause I grew up in musical
theater of being on stage

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.840
and going, "Why is everyone quiet?"

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.250
- [Jon] Yes! (laughing)

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.370
- And they're quiet because
it's your turn to say something.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.240
- Yep.
- Yeah.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.810
- Yep, exactly, exactly.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.146
- That's when I knew the
theater was not for me.

00:01:58.146 --> 00:01:58.979
(Jon laughs)

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:00.720
But anyway, but I heard that,
were you fired from that play?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.400
And was it because you fell asleep?

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.233
- No.
- Okay.

00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:05.423
- Interestingly, I was
fired before I fell asleep.

00:02:05.423 --> 00:02:06.690
(audience laughing)

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.950
So that.
- Wow!

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:08.783
- Yeah, no, no,

00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:10.920
I was actually Matthew
Broderick's understudy

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.690
for a long time.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.940
Well, not for that long
'cause they fired me.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.440
But, but no, it was, that
was my first, first gig.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.650
I was like, I was 18 and I was terrified.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.170
And Matthew is a wonderful,
wonderful performer.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.610
He was the lead in the show.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.510
It was his breakout role.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.983
He won the Tony for it.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.180
And so I was terrified.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.330
And they fired me right
after he won the Tony.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.120
I think because they wanted somebody

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.740
that people had heard of in the show

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.413
taking over for him as opposed to me.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.790
But it was a very formative
experience in my life

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.572
because all of my, my
parents are performers,

00:02:51.572 --> 00:02:54.840
and all of their actors friends
really gathered around me

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.860
because this is the kind of thing,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.503
this happens to actors all the time.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.790
And how you react to it really...

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.290
- [Kelly] Which one, shows who you are.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.530
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.370
- Yeah, and I did the
most constructive thing,

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.448
which was to vow revenge.

00:03:10.448 --> 00:03:12.240
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.220
- You know what though? Sometimes
that's fuel for your fire.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.873
- It was, actually; I did
not prove vow revenge.

00:03:15.873 --> 00:03:17.520
- I'll prove to you like why
you should have picked me

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.460
for that, yeah.
- Exactly.

